    warnings: ['Necrotic spots, expanding blight, canopy loss, and weed co-occurrence are not individually specific to Bipolaris.', 'The seven-to-eight-week onset, middle-canopy predominance, cultivar differences, and combined-disease yield results are study-specific observations, not universal Bipolaris timing, distribution, susceptibility, yield, or action thresholds.', 'The original report used ITS and partial 28S placement, while later multilocus work found multiple genotypes and ploidy states; photographs cannot resolve this diversity.', 'Recovery from a lesion or nearby weed does not by itself prove causation, infection source, or transmission direction.', 'No image or video was indexed because no stable, item-level, plant-linked B. gigantea asset with sufficiently clear reuse and training rights was verified.', 'All symptom-only, detached, mixed-pathogen, culture-unlinked, single-locus-only, low-resolution, and rights-unclear samples require human review.'],
